  "startedAt": "2026-10-12T04:31:09.606Z",
  "steps": [
    "Actual twelve-module/twenty-eight-capability HTTP runtime renders six native-admitted boxes. Fixture covers mixed-axis rotated nonuniform boxes, front/rear occlusion and fully coincident boxes; native UUIDs are verified against source independently of the UI list. Real WebGL2 readPixels records its software renderer.",
    "Actual GPU physical-edge samples show both pale outer pixels and dark inner pixels. Four independent front-face diagonal samples remain exactly unmodified, so triangle diagonals are not highlighted. A selected occluded rear box and selected first-drawn coincident box do not appear through the covering surfaces. Public stable-UUID list selection restores the original same-selection author-camera pixels; no source is written.",
    "Real primary pointer release selects the rotated nonuniform box by stable UUID even outside the name filter, preserving the query and hidden-selection explanation. Empty space and right clicks retain selection. Subthreshold two-pixel pointer jitter selects without orbiting or changing the authored source.",
    "Independent camera-center projection plus real GPU pixels confirm that the nearer front box is selected instead of the occluded rear box. Fully coincident surfaces select the last drawn UUID under the existing LEQUAL depth policy; the actual blue pixel agrees. Author HTML names remain text. This is mathematical box picking, not a pixel-perfect ID buffer claim.",
    "Actual drag beyond the movement threshold orbits without changing selection; real wheel zoom likewise never selects. A qualified real double-click selects and invokes only the existing temporary Focus. GPU hashes change for orbit/focus and Reset restores identical authored-camera pixels with the same selected UUID and the accurate reset status. Source and disk stay unchanged.",
    "Chinese, English and Japanese at 390 px preserve the same filter and stable canvas-selected UUID outside results. A normal modal scroll changes only canvas position, not dimensions; real taps and native double-click still select and focus, including native pointer-capture release/lost-capture order. Public list selection restores the reference UUID before Reset, which restores identical narrow author-camera pixels in that same selection state. True taps also work after responsive redraws; gesture help is translated and the layout has no horizontal overflow.",
    "A canvas-selected UUID uses the existing read-only locator, with native UTF-16 ranges correctly mapped through BOM, CRLF, escaped object keys and preceding astral text. An actual source input immediately blocks old-token location while last-valid visual picking remains usable. Refresh preserves the selected UUID; reversed coincident draw order updates the picked stable identity, and refreshed source navigation resolves its current index.",
    "Explicit ordinary-source fixture deletion removes a model identity and refresh falls back to the first survivor. Invalid newer source retains the last valid rendered model and permits visual picking, with source location still blocked. Closing returns to the editor without implicit Save. Unit tests separately cover pending locator/load and released old-canvas callbacks.",
    "Real native/WASM-admitted near-plane and subpixel-thin source variants render without GL errors. The existing double-sided box exposes its actual back surface after near clipping; selection leaves that same-model center patch strictly unchanged and adds no clipping-plane highlight. A selected 0.001-unit-wide box keeps its stable UUID, while visibility is deliberately not promised for every subpixel or occluded selection. Restoring the original source and UUID exactly restores original GPU pixels; disk bytes remain unchanged.",
    "Explicit WebGL2-unavailable injection disables GPU interaction truthfully while native list selection and exact source location remain available. All preview actions are read-only; saved bytes remain the original fixture, no author/World/execution/Save port is granted, and no installation/device/hardware-GPU claim is made."
  ],
